The question asks whether property hooks (get/set directly in property declaration) were introduced in PHP 8.4.

Let me think about this. Property hooks in PHP were introduced in PHP 8.4. Yes, this is correct. PHP 8.4 introduced "property hooks" which allow you to define get and set behavior directly in the property declaration, like:

```php
class Foo {
    public string $name {
        get => $this->name;
        set => $this->name = (string) $value;
    }
}
```

This was indeed a feature of PHP 8.4, released in November 2024.

So the answer is "да" (yes).
